      "body_plain": "Mmmh... I don't exactly understand what you want to get ultimately,\nbut it looks like your issue is upstream, and it pertains to data\ntransformation before you call joinCountryData2Map.\n\nWhat is it exactly that you want to plot? Do you have this percentage\ncharacters in the data frame itself? Can you give us for instance the\noutput of \"str(wvsneu)\" in R?\n\n   JB\n\nOn Wed, Jul 8, 2015 at 8:12 PM, A.B. <baiera...@gmail.com> wrote:\n> Hi Guys,\n>\n>\n>\n> I want to show the Left-Right self classification from People in countries.\n> So when I take a Cross Table I see how is the Distribution in the Country on\n> the left-right classification. This I want to show on a world map. How can i\n> transform the mean of this cross table and show this on rworld map.\n>\n> I take one plot, but when i compared it with my crosstable, the Distribution\n> is not correct. My R Code are:\n>\n> sPDF <- joinCountryData2Map(wvsneu,\n>                              , joinCode = \"ISO2\"\n>                              , nameJoinColumn = \"iso2c\" )\n> par(mai=c(0,0,0.2,0),xaxs=\"i\",yaxs=\"i\")\n> mapCountryData( sPDF, nameColumnToPlot=\"v95\", addLegend=TRUE,\n>                 mapTitle=\"Selbsteinstufung\", oceanCol=\"lightblue\",\n> missingCountryCol=\"white\"  )\n>\n> and when you compare the results of cross table with my results from plot,\n> then you see the different.\n>\n> Can anyone help me.\n>\n> Thanks in advance!\n>\n> Gisela\n>\n>\n> -------------------------|\n> |                   Count |\n> |             Row Percent |\n> |-------------------------|\n>\n> Total Observations in Table:  59824\n>\n>                     | as.factor(wvs$v95)\n>   as.factor(wvs$v2) |     Left  |        2  |        3  |        4  |\n> 5  |        6  |        7  |        8  |        9  |    Right  | Row Total |\n> --------------------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|-----------|\n> 