      "references": [
        "<HdIk1_OeI_c.ORAv0E9N734J@rworldmap.groups.google.com>",
        "<HdIk1_OeI_c.ZkhyVQLeEHQJ@rworldmap.groups.google.com>"
      ],
      "body_plain": "Hi there,\n\nmapCountryData expects to have only one value per country. In your\ncase you have ten counts per country, that's not one value. So you\nwant to summarize the distribution. But you cannot ask for the \"mean\"\nof a factor. Here we expect \"Left\" to be encoded by 1 and \"Right\" to\nbe encoded as 10, so it seems you took care of giving sound names to\nthe levels of your factor, and then we can go\n\"mean(as.numeric(wvs$v95))\", or simply \"mean(wvs$v95)\", if I assume\nthat in your original data frame these are numerical values. And then\nthat's what you will give mapCountryData to plot, and the actual\ncrosstable is useless.\n\nSo from \"wvs\" or \"wvsneu\", you group by v2 and you summarize by the\nmean of v95 before you give that to plot to mapCountryData. The\ndataframe you give to mapCountryData should have exactly one row per\ncountry.\n\nWith dplyr:\nwvs %>% group_by(v2) %>% summarize(avg=mean(v95)) -> result\nand then you will pass result to joinCountryData2Map and to\nmapCountryData, with nameColumnToPlot=\"avg\"\n\nSee for instance\nhttp://stackoverflow.com/questions/2547402/standard-library-function-in-r-for-finding-the-mode\nin case you want to plot the mode (most frequent value) instead of the\nmean.\n\nGood night,\n   JB\n\nOn Wed, Jul 8, 2015 at 10:20 PM, A.B. <baiera...@gmail.com> wrote:\n> I want to show the mean value of the left-right classification per Country\n> and to show this on a world map.\n>\n> Its the world value Survey Round 6. Its v2 for countrycode and v95 for the\n> left right classification.\n>\n>>\n\n> --\n> You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups\n> \"rworldmap\" group.\n> To post to this group, send email to rwor...@googlegroups.com.\n> Visit this group at http://groups.google.com/group/rworldmap.\n> To view this discussion on the web, visit\n\n> https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/rworldmap/74af4bea-59a3-48b5-a068-b2cd76bc6648%40googlegroups.com.",
      "body_snippet": "Hi there,\n\nmapCountryData expects to have only one value per country. In your\ncase you have ten counts per country, that's not one value. So you\nwant to summarize the distribution. But you cannot ask ",
